{"id":"word:hebrew:H188","type":"word","title":"אוֹי","subtitle":"H188 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"lamentation ; also interjectionally Oh!","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אוֹי (H188) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: inj.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 24 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אוֹי (ʼôwy) means lamentation ; also interjectionally Oh! First listed occurrence: 1Sam 4 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אוֹי","transliteration":"ʼôwy","pronunciation":"o'-ee","strong":"H188","lemmaId":"hebrew:H188","partOfSpeech":"inj","forms":["א֣וֹי","א֥וֹי","אֽוֹי","א֖וֹי","אוֹי"],"morphs":[["HTj",24]]},"definitions":{"short":"lamentation ; also interjectionally Oh!","usage":"alas, woe.","full":"H188. oy אוֺי interjection (onomatopoetic; compare , ) woe! an impassioned expression of grief and despair: usually with dative לִי אוֺי Isa 6:5 woe to me! for I am undone, so 24:16 ; Jer 10:19 ; 15:10 ; לָנוּ אוֺי woe to us! 1Sam 4:7-8 , Jer 4:13 ; 6:4 ; לִי אוֺינָֿא 4:31 ; 45:3 ; לָנוּ אוֺינָֿא Lam 5:16 . With the 2nd or 3rd person often implying a denunciation; מוֺאָב אוֺילְֿךָ Num 21:29 (= Jer 48:46 ) 13:27 ; Ezek 16:23 repeated לָח אוֺי אוֺי ; Isa 3:9 לְנַפְשָׁם אוֺי 3:11 ; Hosea 7:13 ; 9:12 (|| לָהֶם שֹׁד ). With a voc. (or implicit accusative) Ezek 24:6 , 9 הַדָּמִים עִיר אוֺי ; absolute Num 24:23 . Used as a substantive Prov 23:29 אוֺי לְמִי (|| אֲבוֺי לְמִי ).","rootNote":"probably from 183 (in the sense of crying out after);","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 4 7","keyReferences":["1Sam 4 7","1Sam 4 8","Ezek 16 23","Ezek 16 23","Ezek 24 6","Ezek 24 9","Hos 7 13","Hos 9 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":24,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 4 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":4,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"א֣וֹי","so